WEBVTT

00:01.208 --> 00:02.416
[Fisk] Thank you, New York.

00:02.417 --> 00:05.666
It's humbling to be speaking to you
as mayor of this fair city.

00:05.667 --> 00:07.124
The city is in shambles.

00:07.125 --> 00:08.499
A feeling of uneasiness...

00:08.500 --> 00:10.124
- [both grunting]
- ...as if at any moment,

00:10.125 --> 00:11.916
things could explode.

00:11.917 --> 00:12.999
[train screeching]

00:13.000 --> 00:15.125
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:15.750 --> 00:18.499
NYPD. Do not move.

00:18.500 --> 00:20.457
[Fisk] Remember I told you
that I'd get things done?

00:20.458 --> 00:22.499
Well, here I am getting them done.

00:22.500 --> 00:24.457
[Cherry] An NYPD cop is dead.

00:24.458 --> 00:27.041
And anytime that happens,
a big machine gets turned on

00:27.042 --> 00:29.957
to try to figure out what went wrong.
And to punish whoever killed the cop.

00:29.958 --> 00:31.541
[all grunting]

00:31.542 --> 00:32.958
- [bones cracking]
- [officer screams in pain]

00:34.167 --> 00:36.541
[Matt] Do some digging on Hector.
Something doesn't track.

00:36.542 --> 00:39.499
Mr. Ayala, yes or no. Are you
the vigilante known as the White Tiger?

00:39.500 --> 00:41.541
- [gasping]
- [Hochberg] Objection, Your Honor!

00:41.542 --> 00:43.207
- [Judge Cooper] Order!
- [gavel bangs]

00:43.208 --> 00:45.916
[Fisk] These vigilantes,
they are not heroes.

00:45.917 --> 00:48.624
In the matter of
the People v. Hector Ayala,

00:48.625 --> 00:51.374
the jury finds the defendant not guilty.

00:51.375 --> 00:53.207
- [scattered gasps]
- [indistinct chatter]

00:53.208 --> 00:54.874
[♪ dramatic music builds]

00:54.875 --> 00:56.875
- [gun fires]
- [bullet casing clatters]

01:07.792 --> 01:09.792
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:11.958 --> 01:13.292
[keys jangling]

01:14.208 --> 01:16.167
[objects clattering]

01:24.625 --> 01:25.792
[amulet jangling]

01:29.625 --> 01:32.041
- [man] Sorry about your client, Murdock.
- [Matt] Yeah, me too.

01:32.042 --> 01:33.707
So, 9 millimeter to the temple.

01:33.708 --> 01:36.042
Execution style.
No room for error. What else?

01:36.750 --> 01:39.000
[coroner] The right side
marginal abrasion.

01:39.583 --> 01:42.374
External bevel on the entrance wound.
Exit wound has skin tears

01:42.375 --> 01:44.333
- and raised skull fragments.
- Projectile?

01:44.833 --> 01:48.541
Not recovered. High velocity, jacketed.
Maybe even custom.

01:48.542 --> 01:51.207
Single kill shot at extreme close range
and no one found the casing?

01:51.208 --> 01:53.874
Hey. If it's not on the body,
it's not my problem.

01:53.875 --> 01:55.332
[door opens]

01:55.333 --> 01:57.458
- [footsteps approaching]
- [sniffling]

01:59.167 --> 02:00.541
[coroner]
How did you get in here?

02:00.542 --> 02:03.207
- I want to see my uncle, Hector Ayala.
- [coroner sighs]

02:03.208 --> 02:05.875
- You're not supposed to be here.
- [Matt] It's okay, Angela,

02:06.542 --> 02:08.417
- he's right.
- You got him out of jail.

02:09.333 --> 02:10.917
Lotta good that did him, huh?

02:12.583 --> 02:15.832
I wanna see my tío.
I-- I wanna see what they did to him.

02:15.833 --> 02:17.832
You don't, trust me. [breathes deeply]

02:17.833 --> 02:20.041
It's best you remember Hector
the way he was.

02:20.042 --> 02:21.208
Come on. Let's go.

02:25.875 --> 02:27.333
They killed him, didn't they?

02:28.542 --> 02:29.791
- The police.
- [Matt sighs]

02:29.792 --> 02:32.375
We... We don't know.
We don't know that, Angela.

02:32.875 --> 02:35.375
[voice shaking] Come on. You're a lawyer.

02:36.292 --> 02:39.582
You ain't dumb.
He got in the middle of something.

02:39.583 --> 02:42.166
Busted up a fight with his mask off.

02:42.167 --> 02:45.999
Asshole cops were dirty.
You got him out of jail.

02:46.000 --> 02:47.832
They put a bullet through his head.

02:47.833 --> 02:49.374
[breath trembles]

02:49.375 --> 02:52.249
You don't gotta be good at math
to put one and one together, you know?

02:52.250 --> 02:53.333
I know.

02:54.625 --> 02:56.958
- I'm sorry.
- I hate them, Mr. Murdock.

02:57.708 --> 03:00.957
I hate this city.
No one's doing anything about it

03:00.958 --> 03:03.166
and no one's ever gonna do
anything about it,

03:03.167 --> 03:07.083
'cause he was just Hector from the Heights
and they're the fucking cops.

03:09.875 --> 03:10.917
[crying softly]

03:15.042 --> 03:16.167
[sobbing]

03:17.083 --> 03:19.624
It's not fair. [sniffling] It's not fair.

03:19.625 --> 03:21.291
[Matt] I know, I know. It's okay.

03:21.292 --> 03:23.625
It's okay. Look, here, listen.
Listen to me.

03:24.375 --> 03:28.707
You have to believe that someone
will find his killer. Okay?

03:28.708 --> 03:31.625
- We have to believe it. You understand?
- [sniffling]

03:33.167 --> 03:34.582
[Matt sighs]

03:34.583 --> 03:35.667
[softly] Come here.

03:39.292 --> 03:41.292
[horns honking]

03:41.958 --> 03:44.582
[sirens blaring]

03:44.583 --> 03:46.667
[train rattling]

03:48.542 --> 03:50.542
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

03:56.458 --> 03:58.292
- [exhales softly]
- [train rattling]

04:00.458 --> 04:02.458
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

04:07.417 --> 04:09.417
[♪ theme music playing]

05:46.833 --> 05:48.833
[♪ Primaal "Drop da style" playing]

05:54.042 --> 05:55.833
[indistinct chatter]

06:01.708 --> 06:03.375
- [people cheering]
- Oh, shit!

06:05.167 --> 06:06.207
Here you go.

06:06.208 --> 06:07.625
- Thank you.
- Yep.

06:10.958 --> 06:12.166
- Hey!
- [man] Hey!

06:12.167 --> 06:15.916
[all laughing, cheering]

06:15.917 --> 06:17.167
[BB] Shots!

06:18.000 --> 06:20.167
I can't, BB. I think I gotta take off.

06:20.750 --> 06:24.916
No, come on! Dude, Fisk is riding you
way too hard. This whole in by eight--

06:24.917 --> 06:27.166
Seven, actually. So, I gotta go.

06:27.167 --> 06:29.624
Hey, see, this is exactly
what I'm talking about.

06:29.625 --> 06:31.832
Any normal job,
we would take a few more shots,

06:31.833 --> 06:33.957
hit up that spot on 23rd,
sleep on the train,

06:33.958 --> 06:36.207
take a shower, go to work
and do it all over again.

06:36.208 --> 06:39.207
What kind of normal routine is that?
Absolutely not.

06:39.208 --> 06:41.207
Dude, and working for Fisk is?

06:41.208 --> 06:43.249
What can I say? I love the guy.

06:43.250 --> 06:44.333
Oh, God!

06:45.208 --> 06:46.707
No, seriously. Like this afternoon,

06:46.708 --> 06:49.082
we're supposed to meet
with the CleanGreen Haulers.

06:49.083 --> 06:52.249
It's this new tech company with this
dope recycling idea, you know?

06:52.250 --> 06:54.666
- [♪ dance music playing]
- Oh, recycling. That could be cool.

06:54.667 --> 06:57.624
It's awesome.
It would actually decrease garbage output.

06:57.625 --> 06:58.832
Okay, but isn't the problem--

06:58.833 --> 07:01.999
I know you're gonna say
union contracts, but no.

07:02.000 --> 07:05.333
We're gonna start with the ports.
Dual jurisdiction. It's genius.

07:05.958 --> 07:09.792
If we're not gonna keep drinking,
can we at least get some food?

07:10.333 --> 07:12.291
- Absolutely. Yeah. Okay.
- No. I gotta go.

07:12.292 --> 07:13.582
- Come on. We're going.
- Come on.

07:13.583 --> 07:15.417
- I...
- [woman laughs]

07:16.208 --> 07:17.208
[sighs]

07:18.125 --> 07:19.166
[crowd cheering]

07:19.167 --> 07:20.749
[♪ dance music continues]

07:20.750 --> 07:21.874
I am starving.

07:21.875 --> 07:23.582
Ooh, I can go
for some corn cakes right now.

07:23.583 --> 07:25.124
- No, no.
- No, just a quick bite.

07:25.125 --> 07:27.042
I can't, stop making me feel guilty.

07:27.667 --> 07:29.499
- [sighs] Okay. Fine.
- [woman giggling]

07:29.500 --> 07:32.042
Let's get Captain Planet here a cab.

07:34.042 --> 07:35.457
[BB whistles]

07:35.458 --> 07:37.542
[♪ upbeat qawwali
playing over stereo]

07:40.625 --> 07:41.749
Staten Island Ferry.

07:41.750 --> 07:43.332
- [BB] Okay. Bye, grandpa.
- [driver] Got it.

07:43.333 --> 07:44.916
[siren blaring]

07:44.917 --> 07:46.417
[man] No, I didn't do this, man.

07:48.750 --> 07:49.957
[indistinct chatter]

07:49.958 --> 07:51.166
[car door opens]

07:51.167 --> 07:53.291
You want butter toffee
or caramel with peanuts?

07:53.292 --> 07:54.457
Butter toffee.

07:54.458 --> 07:56.666
- Toffee for the man.
- Man, you can't eat that.

07:56.667 --> 07:59.124
Hey, Wilcox. Are these boxes evidence?

07:59.125 --> 08:01.250
Nah. Them other boxes was evidence,
I paid for this shit.

08:02.000 --> 08:05.792
- Hey, seriously. Nothin' for fatty.
- Okay, get your ass up. Let's go.

08:06.750 --> 08:09.082
- Man, get-- I got it, man. Shit.
- Come on.

08:09.083 --> 08:11.166
- Ready? Let's go.
- [man] All right. All right. All right.

08:11.167 --> 08:13.041
- [police over radio] All units...
- [door closes]

08:13.042 --> 08:14.792
[siren blaring]

08:18.208 --> 08:20.957
[female automated voice]
Incoming call from Kirsten.

08:20.958 --> 08:23.874
- [cell phone vibrating]
- Incoming call from Kir--

08:23.875 --> 08:24.958
[cell phone beeps]

08:26.958 --> 08:29.624
- Hey.
- [Kirsten] Hey. Hi, how are you?

08:29.625 --> 08:31.625
I heard Hector's niece came to the morgue.

08:32.542 --> 08:34.000
[Matt] Yeah, it was pretty rough.

08:34.708 --> 08:37.917
- [Kirsten] Did she...
- No. God, no. No kid should see that.

08:38.917 --> 08:41.207
Okay, look, this is terrible timing,

08:41.208 --> 08:43.791
- but I need you downtown today.
- [Matt] Understand.

08:43.792 --> 08:45.041
[inhales deeply] Yeah.

08:45.042 --> 08:48.583
- We'll, uh, post for another associate.
- No. The revolver is too low.

08:49.333 --> 08:52.749
Well, I'm working on that, too. Already
set meetings with a bunch of banks.

08:52.750 --> 08:54.332
Say what you want
about big firms,

08:54.333 --> 08:55.833
but you never have to worry
about money problems.

08:56.458 --> 09:00.582
But you're gonna like this one.
It's Leroy Bradford from the city docket.

09:00.583 --> 09:04.457
I'm underwater on this Madison case
and we owe them a freebie this month.

09:04.458 --> 09:06.416
Can you just meet him down in Detention?

09:06.417 --> 09:09.082
- [Matt] You had me at freebie.
- [chuckles] Thank you.

09:09.083 --> 09:11.166
[♪ tense music playing]

09:11.167 --> 09:12.458
[cell phone thuds]

09:21.000 --> 09:22.417
[indistinct chatter]

09:23.167 --> 09:24.458
[lighter clicks]

09:25.208 --> 09:26.541
[Heather] I thought
we might spend some time

09:26.542 --> 09:29.041
on something we need
to get out into the open.

09:29.042 --> 09:32.124
Until we explore this,
we can't really make any progress.

09:32.125 --> 09:34.041
- Adam...
- I'd rather not.

09:34.042 --> 09:36.332
I understand. [inhales deeply]

09:36.333 --> 09:39.624
But I would urge you
to sit in the discomfort,

09:39.625 --> 09:43.499
and maybe just for a moment,
we can acknowledge the affair.

09:43.500 --> 09:46.292
That's stupid. A ridiculous term.

09:47.667 --> 09:50.083
Not a dinner party. It was betrayal.

09:50.708 --> 09:51.957
[Vanessa scoffs]

09:51.958 --> 09:56.499
You were gone. I didn't know
when or if you were ever coming back.

09:56.500 --> 09:59.541
You knew. You know me,
you knew I wouldn't stay away.

09:59.542 --> 10:01.999
You left. That was a betrayal.

10:02.000 --> 10:05.167
- [Fisk] You know why--
- Let's let Vanessa speak for a moment.

10:05.792 --> 10:06.917
Tell me about Adam.

10:07.625 --> 10:09.250
- You're asking for details?
- [Heather] No.

10:10.083 --> 10:11.458
I'm curious about you.

10:12.750 --> 10:15.083
What you were feeling. Why him?

10:15.917 --> 10:17.000
[Vanessa sighs]

10:18.917 --> 10:20.292
It was his hands.

10:22.292 --> 10:24.375
His hands drew...

10:25.792 --> 10:29.291
- beautiful sketches. I mean, just--
- Can we not?

10:29.292 --> 10:34.667
It was like finding a Klee
at a garage sale. It was just...

10:36.000 --> 10:37.000
[sighs]

10:38.333 --> 10:41.000
[clicks tongue] He wasn't part
of my husband's world.

10:41.625 --> 10:44.374
And what world is that? Politics?

10:44.375 --> 10:45.583
[both] Business.

10:46.917 --> 10:47.917
I see.

10:50.292 --> 10:52.749
Has infidelity been a part
of your marriage before this?

10:52.750 --> 10:54.416
- Absolutely not. Never.
- [Vanessa scoffs]

10:54.417 --> 10:55.542
You left.

10:56.917 --> 10:59.332
Which felt like taking half of me away.

10:59.333 --> 11:01.417
[♪ tense music playing]

11:02.333 --> 11:04.417
Did that trigger something
for you, Vanessa?

11:06.542 --> 11:07.750
My father...

11:10.542 --> 11:12.082
he was in textiles.

11:12.083 --> 11:14.041
[♪ melancholy music playing]

11:14.042 --> 11:16.500
He would leave for weeks at a time.

11:18.000 --> 11:19.000
He drank.

11:19.625 --> 11:21.874
He, uh, gambled.

11:21.875 --> 11:24.208
His behavior ate at my mother.

11:25.583 --> 11:26.583
Crushed her.

11:27.250 --> 11:29.375
I never respected her for that.

11:30.250 --> 11:31.583
[breath trembles]

11:32.917 --> 11:36.333
I needed to feel alive. Not crushed down.

11:38.792 --> 11:40.167
When you left, you hurt me.

11:40.708 --> 11:42.207
You never told me.

11:42.208 --> 11:44.042
I never had a reason to.

11:45.042 --> 11:46.833
I assume you wanna move forward from this.

11:48.000 --> 11:50.667
- Did you end the affair?
- I never had the opportunity.

11:53.708 --> 11:55.542
Why not? Did something happen?

11:57.375 --> 11:59.458
Wilson, did you confront this man?

12:00.708 --> 12:01.708
Yes.

12:03.167 --> 12:04.291
We had a dialogue.

12:04.292 --> 12:06.291
[♪ tense music playing]

12:06.292 --> 12:07.667
[Heather] What kind of dialogue?

12:10.792 --> 12:11.958
A clarifying one.

12:12.958 --> 12:15.125
- Would you like to be more specific?
- No.

12:16.125 --> 12:18.207
[Vanessa] Oh...
So that's what we're doing here.

12:18.208 --> 12:20.374
This is just window dressing.

12:20.375 --> 12:22.707
I know you,
your methods are much more direct.

12:22.708 --> 12:25.333
No. They were, not now.
It was a conversation.

12:25.917 --> 12:28.750
That's all.
There was no expression of ill intent.

12:30.167 --> 12:32.042
I did tell him how I felt about you.

12:33.958 --> 12:35.625
About our marriage.

12:37.792 --> 12:39.000
And I told him...

12:40.333 --> 12:42.000
[voice trembling]
...that I couldn't fathom

12:43.417 --> 12:46.416
a life of meaning without her.

12:46.417 --> 12:48.667
[♪ somber music playing]

12:49.875 --> 12:52.125
- [Fisk sighs]
- And where is Adam now?

12:53.208 --> 12:54.625
[both] I don't know.

12:58.750 --> 13:02.207
I wanna go back to the first question
I asked you during our intake.

13:02.208 --> 13:06.499
"Are we here to dissolve a marriage
or preserve one?"

13:06.500 --> 13:08.208
I want you to think about it.

13:09.167 --> 13:11.208
Really think about it
before I see you again.

13:12.208 --> 13:14.999
Without forgiveness,
and I say this to both of you,

13:15.000 --> 13:16.750
there can be no real healing.

13:17.542 --> 13:20.874
Forgiveness isn't just
the highest act of love,

13:20.875 --> 13:22.750
it is the only way forward.

13:25.083 --> 13:26.208
Good work today.

13:26.833 --> 13:27.875
[Heather clears throat]

13:31.917 --> 13:35.666
If you two don't mind, I'd love to speak
to Vanessa alone for a moment please.

13:35.667 --> 13:36.750
Just the two of us.

13:49.208 --> 13:50.833
Is something wrong, Dr. Glenn?

13:51.667 --> 13:52.666
I'm not sure.

13:52.667 --> 13:57.458
Based on the nature of our discussion
today, I feel obligated to ask...

13:59.667 --> 14:01.125
Do you feel safe in your marriage?

14:02.750 --> 14:04.832
Oh... You think...

14:04.833 --> 14:06.917
[♪ tense music playing]

14:07.833 --> 14:08.958
How sweet of you.

14:10.375 --> 14:11.417
[chuckles softly]

14:12.833 --> 14:16.542
My husband is capable of many,
many things, some of them extreme.

14:17.250 --> 14:19.750
Harming me is not one of them.

14:25.125 --> 14:26.125
[door opens]

14:26.833 --> 14:27.957
[pigeon coos]

14:27.958 --> 14:29.832
[indistinct chatter]

14:29.833 --> 14:31.249
[car honking]

14:31.250 --> 14:34.874
[man] Mayor Fisk. He might be a nice guy,
but I think he's in over his head.

14:34.875 --> 14:38.082
Vigilantes, love 'em.
Should've had that a long time ago.

14:38.083 --> 14:40.916
They're the only people
that can solve the problem in New York.

14:40.917 --> 14:43.708
I wish I could be a vigilante,
I'd be out there, too.

14:49.875 --> 14:51.666
[indistinct conversations]

14:51.667 --> 14:54.417
Leroy Bradford? Is there a Leroy Bradford?

14:59.333 --> 15:03.332
Man, look at this.
I get the freakin' blind dude.

15:03.333 --> 15:05.042
[men laugh]

15:06.083 --> 15:07.542
- Let's go.
- [Leroy scoffs]

15:08.250 --> 15:10.292
Bring on the blind justice.

15:11.000 --> 15:12.291
[door squeaks, closes]

15:12.292 --> 15:13.958
[door buzzing]

15:14.583 --> 15:17.916
Mr. Bradford, my name is Matthew Murdock,
I'm gonna be your lawyer.

15:17.917 --> 15:19.249
[Leroy] Lucky me.

15:19.250 --> 15:22.624
As I understand it, you've been charged
with petty larceny, a class A misdemeanor.

15:22.625 --> 15:25.541
The complaint against you alleges
you stole approximately five boxes

15:25.542 --> 15:28.125
- of Fiddle Faddle from a bodega.
- Well, I didn't do it.

15:28.625 --> 15:30.999
- Uh... Okay.
- I said, I didn't do that shit!

15:31.000 --> 15:34.082
I understand. The thing is,
the bodega where this allegedly occurred

15:34.083 --> 15:37.083
has a surveillance system,
involving many cameras.

15:37.792 --> 15:40.041
They've already turned over
to the prosecution footage

15:40.042 --> 15:42.166
which they claim shows you
stealing the items.

15:42.167 --> 15:44.707
In addition, the cashier
is willing to testify

15:44.708 --> 15:46.874
she was an eyewitness to the whole thing,

15:46.875 --> 15:49.624
and the store security guard
will testify that when he detained you,

15:49.625 --> 15:52.917
you were in possession of multiple boxes
of Fiddle Faddle caramel corn.

15:54.667 --> 15:56.249
Uh, finally, the police will corroborate

15:56.250 --> 15:58.999
that several boxes of the caramel corn
were recovered outside of the store.

15:59.000 --> 16:01.666
Look, I paid for that shit last week.

16:01.667 --> 16:04.291
Unfortunately, it doesn't really
work like that, Mr. Bradford.

16:04.292 --> 16:06.457
Generally, you pay
for what you buy that day.

16:06.458 --> 16:08.292
Then they all lying on me, then.

16:10.458 --> 16:11.499
You hear me?

16:11.500 --> 16:12.708
Um...

16:13.167 --> 16:15.707
Also, I saw them cops
eatin' two boxes of that shit.

16:15.708 --> 16:17.457
Now that I'm entirely willing to believe.

16:17.458 --> 16:19.832
Then how come they don't arrest
themselves for stealing?

16:19.833 --> 16:21.249
Maybe they should have.

16:21.250 --> 16:24.832
Uh, but the complexity of that aside,
we're here 'cause they arrested you.

16:24.833 --> 16:26.292
[sighs]

16:27.625 --> 16:28.792
Could it have been a Skrull?

16:30.458 --> 16:31.624
[smacks lips] Nope.

16:31.625 --> 16:34.166
And the bigger problem
we have is your rap sheet.

16:34.167 --> 16:36.666
How come you guys
always gotta bring that up?

16:36.667 --> 16:39.124
What I did back then ain't got
nothing to do with this.

16:39.125 --> 16:41.582
That's true, but when a judge
sees a sheet like yours,

16:41.583 --> 16:46.082
20, 25 pages of offenses, drugs,
trespassing, panhandling, petty larceny,

16:46.083 --> 16:49.166
not to mention the four separate cases
where you failed to appear in court,

16:49.167 --> 16:50.999
and they had to issue a bench warrant.

16:51.000 --> 16:52.333
I gotta get home, man.

16:53.125 --> 16:54.874
Like I said, I ain't going to jail.

16:54.875 --> 16:58.499
If you decide to fight the case,
with the video evidence,

16:58.500 --> 17:00.457
your rap sheet, history of bench warrants,

17:00.458 --> 17:03.249
the judge will almost certainly set bail.
Which means unless you can pay the bail--

17:03.250 --> 17:04.499
I look like I got money to you?

17:04.500 --> 17:06.457
You're gonna sit in jail
until this whole thing is over.

17:06.458 --> 17:08.291
So what're you trying to tell me to do?

17:08.292 --> 17:10.832
- Cop out? You a cop out lawyer?
- If you take a plea--

17:10.833 --> 17:12.333
No. No!

17:13.917 --> 17:16.624
Look, man, you even think
about telling me to cop out--

17:16.625 --> 17:18.666
You better go out there
and get me my probation.

17:18.667 --> 17:20.082
I'm gonna really try here, Leroy.

17:20.083 --> 17:22.916
Let me be clear,
probation is not gonna be on the table.

17:22.917 --> 17:24.167
Then I ain't takin' it.

17:24.583 --> 17:25.874
Last time you got arrested for stealing,

17:25.875 --> 17:27.916
- you got a 30-day sentence.
- Mmm-hmm.

17:27.917 --> 17:29.582
Which means the DA's office
is almost certainly

17:29.583 --> 17:31.249
gonna offer something
in excess of 30 days.

17:31.250 --> 17:33.874
- Is 30 the same as probation?
- Nope, on 30 you do 20.

17:33.875 --> 17:37.666
- Then I ain't takin' it!
- In which case we're gonna have to talk--

17:37.667 --> 17:40.749
Look, I don't wanna hear no more shit
about "in which case"!

17:40.750 --> 17:43.750
This is my case, and I'm goin' home on it.

17:44.333 --> 17:47.249
- You hear me, blind man?
- Loud and clear.

17:47.250 --> 17:50.332
Then go out there and do your job
and get me some probation.

17:50.333 --> 17:51.541
[breathes deeply]

17:51.542 --> 17:54.958
- Yeah, let me, uh, see what I can do.
- See? [laughs]

17:56.167 --> 17:59.292
See, that's funny,
'cause you can't see shit!

17:59.958 --> 18:01.125
[chuckles]

18:02.083 --> 18:03.167
[Leroy laughs]

18:04.292 --> 18:06.207
I'm not gonna do this...
[continues indistinctly]

18:06.208 --> 18:07.791
- [Matt] Sorry.
- What you got, Murdock?

18:07.792 --> 18:10.541
Morning, Sofija.
I'm sure you look lovely today.

18:10.542 --> 18:13.166
- Uh, 8357, Bradford.
- [indistinct chatter]

18:13.167 --> 18:14.917
Oh... Yeah.

18:15.833 --> 18:17.791
Stole some caramel corn
from the bodega.

18:17.792 --> 18:18.874
Yep, that's the guy.

18:18.875 --> 18:22.749
Looks like we went 30 days on this
the last time, so how about we go 35?

18:22.750 --> 18:24.332
So, the guy's looking for probation.

18:24.333 --> 18:26.624
- And I'm looking for Mr. Right.
- [chuckles]

18:26.625 --> 18:29.082
- You're not him by any chance, are you?
- Maybe for probation.

18:29.083 --> 18:32.374
Or how about you remind your client
that the whole point of deterrents...

18:32.375 --> 18:34.957
A totally discredited penal philosophy,
by the way, but okay.

18:34.958 --> 18:39.999
...is that sentences go up, and not down,
when you continue to commit crimes.

18:40.000 --> 18:41.249
Also, deterrence works.

18:41.250 --> 18:44.666
- His rap sheet would suggest otherwise.
- Maybe we haven't been harsh enough.

18:44.667 --> 18:46.416
Or maybe the whole idea
relies on the theory that

18:46.417 --> 18:48.791
people are actually thinking about
the consequences of their actions,

18:48.792 --> 18:49.874
which I can assure you,

18:49.875 --> 18:52.958
having spent a full five minutes
with Mr. Bradford, he was not.

18:53.875 --> 18:56.207
Can I go five days community service
on the trespass?

18:56.208 --> 18:59.082
Sure. Well, uh,
if... if you don't like deterrents,

18:59.083 --> 19:03.124
how about incapacitation? Let's just
keep him off the streets for 35 days.

19:03.125 --> 19:04.707
Come on, Sofija,
you really wanna prove a point

19:04.708 --> 19:07.541
over some stolen caramel corn
on Latvian Heritage Day?

19:07.542 --> 19:09.082
How'd you know I was Latvian?

19:09.083 --> 19:11.417
Pretty sure you snuck a piece
of honey cake for breakfast.

19:12.125 --> 19:13.124
- Wow.
- [Matt] It's a blind thing.

19:13.125 --> 19:15.249
- [Sofija] Mmm.
- You know, heightened senses and all.

19:15.250 --> 19:18.082
Mmm. I can imagine wanting to know
a little bit more about that.

19:18.083 --> 19:19.875
[chuckles] Plus, with a name like Ozola...

19:21.042 --> 19:23.249
Well, [clears throat]
given your cultural sensitivity

19:23.250 --> 19:24.541
and your very impressive nose,

19:24.542 --> 19:25.791
I'll give your guy 20 days.

19:25.792 --> 19:27.374
Mmm...

19:27.375 --> 19:29.166
He's really stuck on probation.

19:29.167 --> 19:30.957
Did you remind him that the last time

19:30.958 --> 19:33.082
that he actually got probation,
which was by the way,

19:33.083 --> 19:34.999
- 11 cases ago by my count...
- Yeah.

19:35.000 --> 19:38.499
It only took him two months before his PO
violated him for failure to report?

19:38.500 --> 19:40.291
What can I say?
The guy has strong preferences.

19:40.292 --> 19:41.500
Yeah, well, so do I.

19:42.167 --> 19:43.832
So, how about this 20 days?

19:43.833 --> 19:46.916
On which he does 15, minus today.
You're really saying

19:46.917 --> 19:48.374
from a philosophical point of view,

19:48.375 --> 19:50.541
- two weeks as opposed to probation?
- [laughs]

19:50.542 --> 19:53.749
Only you, Murdock. Arguing philosophy
in criminal court arraignments.

19:53.750 --> 19:56.874
You started it. And while we're on it,
isn't it worth pointing out

19:56.875 --> 19:59.582
that the name of the crime we're dealing
with here is "petty larceny"?

19:59.583 --> 20:01.291
From the French, petit. Meaning...

20:01.292 --> 20:04.082
All right, one time only,
last and final offer.

20:04.083 --> 20:06.292
- Mr. Bradford can have ten days.
- Yes!

20:07.208 --> 20:08.207
Thank you.

20:08.208 --> 20:10.792
- See, I knew you believed in redemption.
- Oh, I don't. I don't.

20:11.542 --> 20:14.207
- But I do hope he appreciates you.
- [Matt] Thank you.

20:14.208 --> 20:15.833
[indistinct conversations]

20:24.083 --> 20:26.167
[man] What? No.

20:27.417 --> 20:28.417
What?

20:29.875 --> 20:30.875
Who?

20:32.167 --> 20:35.624
No, no, that guy's an idiot. No, no,
just you. Just you there at six o'clock.

20:35.625 --> 20:39.082
Officer Powell?
I thought I recognized that voice.

20:39.083 --> 20:40.375
Shit, I gotta go.

20:41.583 --> 20:43.166
Counselor Murdock. Funny how we keep

20:43.167 --> 20:45.083
- finding each other like this.
- Yeah. Isn't it?

20:45.917 --> 20:48.042
You, uh, doing the Lord's work today?

20:49.250 --> 20:50.250
Yeah.

20:50.958 --> 20:53.416
Hey, you couldn't have
a weak link out there, could you?

20:53.417 --> 20:55.541
- What?
- Or, I don't know, maybe it was pride.

20:55.542 --> 20:57.082
Ayala made you look bad, didn't he?

20:57.083 --> 20:59.082
[chuckling] Actually,
he flat out embarrassed you,

20:59.083 --> 21:02.582
and you can't have that at the NYPD.
Is that why you did it?

21:02.583 --> 21:04.667
[♪ tense music playing]

21:05.917 --> 21:07.541
[clears throat] You have yourself
a nice day, Counselor.

21:07.542 --> 21:08.667
He had a family.

21:09.292 --> 21:11.750
He had a future.
And you took that away from him.

21:12.458 --> 21:14.417
[Powell breathes deeply]

21:17.083 --> 21:19.416
You can't see this badge, Counselor,
'cause you're fuckin' blind,

21:19.417 --> 21:21.583
but my grandfather wore this badge,

21:22.208 --> 21:24.791
my father wore this badge,
my brother wears this badge,

21:24.792 --> 21:27.041
four of my fuckin' cousins
wear this badge,

21:27.042 --> 21:29.041
they're all knuckleheads,
but they're good cops.

21:29.042 --> 21:30.666
So I wear this fucking badge
with honor, Counselor.

21:30.667 --> 21:31.749
[heart thumping]

21:31.750 --> 21:36.124
And I don't know nothin' about nothin'
to do with what happened to Hector Ayala.

21:36.125 --> 21:38.417
[heart thumping rhythmically]

21:42.708 --> 21:44.125
But here's somethin' that I know.

21:44.917 --> 21:47.791
An attorney who assaults
a police officer? [scoffs]

21:47.792 --> 21:50.042
Who obstructs an active investigation?

21:50.708 --> 21:53.041
Not somethin' that
the Bar Association's gonna take lightly

21:53.042 --> 21:54.624
- if you catch my meaning.
- [chuckles] Mmm.

21:54.625 --> 21:57.082
Not to mention some of my more
excitable colleagues

21:57.083 --> 21:58.582
- on the force.
- Ah, yeah.

21:58.583 --> 22:03.125
Only... you'd have to bring a few more
than the last time we met, wouldn't you?

22:05.208 --> 22:07.625
All right. I'll be seein' you, Counselor.

22:08.542 --> 22:10.542
[♪ tense music playing]

22:13.000 --> 22:14.708
[water splashing]

22:16.458 --> 22:18.542
- [seagulls squawking]
- [Fisk] New York City.

22:20.583 --> 22:22.167
The greatest city on Earth.

22:23.375 --> 22:25.958
The heart of finance, publishing.

22:26.500 --> 22:28.250
International diplomacy.

22:30.250 --> 22:33.458
But I think we've lost something
along the way.

22:36.125 --> 22:37.250
Industry.

22:38.333 --> 22:40.292
The pride of the working class.

22:40.917 --> 22:43.249
If I say Red Hook,
what words come to mind?

22:43.250 --> 22:44.916
- Graves.
- Decrepit.

22:44.917 --> 22:46.207
I mean, it's dirty, too.

22:46.208 --> 22:49.832
Yes. This port is a black eye
on the face of this city.

22:49.833 --> 22:51.207
[foghorn blares]

22:51.208 --> 22:52.792
Has been for a while.

22:54.542 --> 22:56.125
I think we can do better.

22:57.292 --> 23:00.207
I'm talkin' about a complete
structural overhaul.

23:00.208 --> 23:02.500
- That's not an option.
- A total transformation.

23:03.250 --> 23:06.041
I told the people of this city I was gonna
come out of the gate strong,

23:06.042 --> 23:07.666
that's exactly what I'm gonna do.

23:07.667 --> 23:10.041
Hell yeah, sir.

23:10.042 --> 23:13.750
Daniel, I want you
to organize a press conference.

23:15.125 --> 23:16.707
I wanna get this message out immediately.

23:16.708 --> 23:18.874
With all due respect,

23:18.875 --> 23:21.957
you can't just decide something
and then speak it into existence.

23:21.958 --> 23:23.291
[Fisk] And why is that, Sheila?

23:23.292 --> 23:25.832
This is city government.
There are processes.

23:25.833 --> 23:27.375
Yes, processes.

23:28.667 --> 23:30.708
I don't have much use for red tape.

23:31.375 --> 23:34.499
I know you're used
to a different approach,

23:34.500 --> 23:37.207
but that's not how
it works in this office.

23:37.208 --> 23:39.707
These things take time, patience.

23:39.708 --> 23:41.207
[Fisk] What's your opinion, Daniel?

23:41.208 --> 23:43.749
[Sheila] Opinions are above his pay grade.

23:43.750 --> 23:47.750
Besides, there was another mob shooting
yesterday not 50 feet from here.

23:48.250 --> 23:52.082
The third one this month.
The violence makes people uneasy.

23:52.083 --> 23:55.291
This is an ambitious goal.
It's a worthy goal,

23:55.292 --> 23:59.499
I'm not saying we shouldn't do it,
I'm just saying we need to start smaller.

23:59.500 --> 24:01.332
That could be our next campaign slogan.

24:01.333 --> 24:02.500
[sighs]

24:03.708 --> 24:07.917
I hear you saying
that my plan is improbable,

24:08.500 --> 24:10.000
but not impossible.

24:10.458 --> 24:11.750
You're giving me problems.

24:13.000 --> 24:14.542
I want solutions.

24:16.583 --> 24:17.708
Where do we start?

24:18.750 --> 24:24.832
[sighs] I suppose we would need
to conduct a feasibility study.

24:24.833 --> 24:28.791
Land surveys,
building permits, zoning laws.

24:28.792 --> 24:32.666
Environmental impact. Um, traffic issues.

24:32.667 --> 24:35.791
The council will want to know
that this project is viable.

24:35.792 --> 24:37.124
Yes, let's commission that study.

24:37.125 --> 24:39.207
We can't do that
without the council's approval.

24:39.208 --> 24:40.582
- Then get the council to--
- No.

24:40.583 --> 24:43.416
[smacks lips] And we can't get
their approval until we ask

24:43.417 --> 24:46.042
the public advocate
to put it on the docket.

24:46.583 --> 24:48.457
- That's the first step?
- Yes, sir.

24:48.458 --> 24:50.125
Let's take that step.

24:51.125 --> 24:52.332
Yes, sir.

24:52.333 --> 24:55.582
In the meantime, sir,
we do have a full day in front of us.

24:55.583 --> 24:57.957
[Fisk] Full days, I like. I'm all yours.

24:57.958 --> 24:59.042
[Fisk chuckles softly]

25:01.542 --> 25:04.332
- Uh, thank you, Mr. Mayor.
- [Fisk] Yes.

25:04.333 --> 25:06.458
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

25:08.500 --> 25:12.000
I... I was basically gonna say
everything that you did, so...

25:13.792 --> 25:16.582
[Buck sighs] She's right about one thing.

25:16.583 --> 25:19.457
Now what's happening down here
is a bigger problem than you realize.

25:19.458 --> 25:22.124
The other bosses will continue
to create havoc

25:22.125 --> 25:26.083
until one of them is sentenced
or they all die.

25:27.375 --> 25:29.375
[♪ ominous music playing]

25:32.917 --> 25:34.416
- [door opens]
- [Matt exhales]

25:34.417 --> 25:36.999
- [Matt] Great news. [clears throat]
- You got me that probation.

25:37.000 --> 25:39.874
Nope. I got you ten days,
on which you do seven, minus today,

25:39.875 --> 25:42.124
you get the weekend bounce back
and you are out on Friday.

25:42.125 --> 25:44.249
- How is that great news?
- [Matt] Come on, Leroy,

25:44.250 --> 25:47.374
the least you've gotten
in your last ten cases is 20 days.

25:47.375 --> 25:49.707
Anything below 30 is a gift,
ten is a miracle.

25:49.708 --> 25:51.874
Look, I said probation,
and I meant probation!

25:51.875 --> 25:53.624
You took the stuff, Leroy.

25:53.625 --> 25:56.666
There is no probation to be had here.
This is the best deal you're gonna get,

25:56.667 --> 25:59.166
so you tell me, how is this not
a "Good job, counselor" situation?

25:59.167 --> 26:03.083
So, you just wanna shove my ass into jail
and I'm supposed to thank you?

26:04.542 --> 26:06.375
You just don't get it, do you?

26:07.500 --> 26:09.375
This shit never ends!

26:10.375 --> 26:12.958
I've been jerked around
by the system my whole life.

26:13.583 --> 26:16.375
Last time I got 30 days,
know what happened?

26:17.625 --> 26:21.250
I missed my SSI appointment
and they cut my benefits.

26:22.792 --> 26:26.000
Bad enough trying to live off food stamps,
but when they cut it,

26:26.625 --> 26:29.250
man, it takes forever
to get that shit back regular.

26:31.125 --> 26:33.124
[♪ somber choral music playing]

26:33.125 --> 26:37.875
Then you gotta start eating throw away
crap from supermarket dumpsters,

26:40.083 --> 26:42.042
begging for change,

26:42.750 --> 26:43.875
for food.

26:46.417 --> 26:49.208
And yeah, just once,

26:50.375 --> 26:51.625
I want a dessert.

26:52.500 --> 26:56.750
Something that don't taste like crap.
Something that tastes real good.

26:59.000 --> 27:00.875
So, why'd I get the caramel corn?

27:02.417 --> 27:04.792
I like that shit, and it tastes good.

27:06.750 --> 27:10.207
And for that, they're willing
to spend five times more

27:10.208 --> 27:13.250
to lock me up than they are willing
to spend to feed me.

27:14.542 --> 27:17.333
And you come in here
and tell me that that's a gift?

27:18.542 --> 27:20.042
That I should thank you?

27:22.875 --> 27:23.917
You're right.

27:25.250 --> 27:26.457
[sighs]

27:26.458 --> 27:28.542
[♪ somber music playing]

27:30.625 --> 27:31.667
[breathes deeply]

27:34.500 --> 27:36.458
It don't matter anyway. [sighs]

27:41.667 --> 27:42.957
[choir teacher] A one, two, three and...

27:42.958 --> 27:46.124
[children singing discordantly]
♪ We built this city ♪

27:46.125 --> 27:49.957
♪ We built this city on rock and roll ♪

27:49.958 --> 27:51.958
♪ Built this city ♪

27:53.125 --> 27:57.624
- ♪ We built this city on rock and roll ♪
- ♪ And roll ♪

27:57.625 --> 27:58.875
[cell phone vibrates]

28:00.083 --> 28:05.874
♪ Marconi plays the mamba
Listen to the radio ♪

28:05.875 --> 28:08.749
♪ Don't you remember? ♪

28:08.750 --> 28:10.374
♪ We built this city... ♪

28:10.375 --> 28:11.916
There's somethin' I need to show you.

28:11.917 --> 28:14.541
♪ We built this city on rock... ♪

28:14.542 --> 28:17.416
- Ma'am, you have to see this.
- Just spit it out, Daniel. What?

28:17.417 --> 28:20.166
♪ We built this city
We built this city ♪

28:20.167 --> 28:21.916
♪ We built this city... ♪

28:21.917 --> 28:24.625
It was me. I totally screwed up.

28:25.125 --> 28:27.457
- [Sheila] You did this?
- [Daniel] It was a mistake.

28:27.458 --> 28:29.499
- I... I went out and I--
- You know what?

28:29.500 --> 28:30.625
I don't wanna hear it.

28:32.667 --> 28:36.250
Just call the schedulers and have them
pull the meeting off the calendar. Now.

28:36.917 --> 28:39.166
- I'm sorry.
- I said "now," Daniel.

28:39.167 --> 28:40.666
[singing continues]

28:40.667 --> 28:41.875
[Daniel] Yes, ma'am. Got you.

28:42.667 --> 28:45.999
♪ We built this city ♪

28:46.000 --> 28:48.625
- How are we gonna fix that? I mean--
- There is no we.

28:49.125 --> 28:50.999
I was here before you and before Fisk,

28:51.000 --> 28:53.541
and I will be here long
after you're both gone.

28:53.542 --> 28:55.957
I will handle it, understand?

28:55.958 --> 28:57.499
You just keep your mouth shut.

28:57.500 --> 29:00.832
♪ We built this city, we built this city ♪

29:00.833 --> 29:04.166
♪ We built
We built this city ♪

29:04.167 --> 29:08.457
♪ On rock and roll ♪

29:08.458 --> 29:10.332
[applause]

29:10.333 --> 29:12.000
Just wonderful.

29:12.583 --> 29:14.291
Children have such talent.

29:14.292 --> 29:18.666
Thank you, Mr. Mayor.
Now, for our next one--

29:18.667 --> 29:21.916
No, no, no. No, that's... that's...
that's fine. Fine.

29:21.917 --> 29:23.708
Such talent. And, again,

29:24.583 --> 29:26.500
you were wonderful. And, uh...

29:27.000 --> 29:30.125
as they say, "the city never sleeps."

29:30.542 --> 29:33.041
[applause]

29:33.042 --> 29:34.250
[horns honking]

29:36.083 --> 29:38.499
Everything ready
for the CleanGreen Haulers meeting?

29:38.500 --> 29:41.291
Actually, sir, we've had
to pull that off the calendar.

29:41.292 --> 29:43.458
- There's a small wrinkle.
- What's that?

29:45.083 --> 29:46.499
They're calling you a union buster,

29:46.500 --> 29:49.042
so we've broomed the meeting
off the schedule.

29:49.708 --> 29:52.499
We can do it quietly in a neutral place
sometime soon.

29:52.500 --> 29:53.749
Somebody screwed up.

29:53.750 --> 29:54.916
Leaks happen.

29:54.917 --> 29:56.875
Not in my administration it doesn't.

29:57.625 --> 30:00.625
[breathes deeply] I want
an all hands meeting. Now!

30:01.708 --> 30:03.082
Where am I?

30:03.083 --> 30:04.832
It's the Latvian Cultural Center.

30:04.833 --> 30:08.207
It's on your calendar.
Latvian Heritage Day?

30:08.208 --> 30:10.749
[Fisk] What do I care
about Latvian Heritage?

30:10.750 --> 30:13.791
You care because
it is an important constituency.

30:13.792 --> 30:15.499
- [Fisk sighs]
- You won by 16 points

30:15.500 --> 30:17.249
which actually mattered in Queens.

30:17.250 --> 30:18.583
[Fisk] I'm not in the mood.

30:19.375 --> 30:21.832
Respectfully, Mr. Mayor, this is the job.

30:21.833 --> 30:24.457
[host] Ladies and gentlemen,
and honored guests,

30:24.458 --> 30:28.249
I present to you, the Mayor
of New York City, Wilson Fisk.

30:28.250 --> 30:30.667
- [applause]
- [choir singing in Latvian]

30:44.083 --> 30:45.833
[shouts] "Mayor Garbage?"
Is that it?

30:46.500 --> 30:47.542
Is that your best?

30:48.542 --> 30:53.082
You are all here to help me
execute my promises.

30:53.083 --> 30:56.499
My promises to the people!
Simple promises!

30:56.500 --> 31:00.166
I will find out
which one of you leaked this.

31:00.167 --> 31:01.624
I will find out!

31:01.625 --> 31:04.332
It was me, sir. I screwed up.

31:04.333 --> 31:05.582
[whispers] Damn it.

31:05.583 --> 31:09.041
[Daniel] I completely made a mistake.
This entire thing is my fault.

31:09.042 --> 31:10.667
[Fisk breathes heavily]

31:12.917 --> 31:14.708
Everybody out! Out!

31:17.917 --> 31:19.417
You stay! Right here.

31:20.292 --> 31:21.458
Sheila, I said out.

31:22.792 --> 31:25.457
He's mine, sir.
Whatever he did, it's on me.

31:25.458 --> 31:28.416
Okay, fine. Suit yourself.
You can go down with the ship.

31:28.417 --> 31:31.332
I... I wanna apologize,
I didn't mean to do it.

31:31.333 --> 31:34.332
I know that won't make it right.
I know that nothing can.

31:34.333 --> 31:38.041
But I went out to a club
till 4:30, maybe even 5:00,

31:38.042 --> 31:41.916
and I had a couple of...
Look, I had a lot to drink,

31:41.917 --> 31:45.374
tequila and in the spirit
of total honesty,

31:45.375 --> 31:48.291
- there was some ketamine.
- You should probably stop.

31:48.292 --> 31:50.749
I was drunk and stupid and I didn't mean
to do it, but I did do it,

31:50.750 --> 31:54.249
and I know that's unforgivable,
and I'm not even asking for forgiveness,

31:54.250 --> 31:56.708
because... [scoffs]
I can't even forgive myself...

31:57.458 --> 31:59.667
'cause... 'cause the thing is,
you're right.

32:00.458 --> 32:03.875
I don't deserve this job. And I never did.

32:05.208 --> 32:09.333
So, you're right to fire me or punish me
or do whatever you're gonna do.

32:11.083 --> 32:14.042
And I just...
I wanna say that I'm eternally loyal

32:15.083 --> 32:17.707
and forever grateful for the opportunity

32:17.708 --> 32:20.958
and I'll spend the rest of my life
regretting how badly I screwed it up.

32:21.833 --> 32:23.958
I... I believe in you.

32:24.792 --> 32:28.457
You'll have my vote forever
and whatever happens to me,

32:28.458 --> 32:30.082
I'll do whatever I can from afar

32:30.083 --> 32:33.458
to support you and your mayorship.

32:35.875 --> 32:37.750
[Fisk sighs]

32:42.208 --> 32:44.666
Yeah, I'm... I'm not gonna fire you.

32:44.667 --> 32:46.207
I'll pack my things right away, sir.

32:46.208 --> 32:47.750
I said, I'm not gonna fire you.

32:48.917 --> 32:49.917
Or you, Sheila.

32:51.333 --> 32:54.542
I've been around a lot of,
let's just say...

32:55.542 --> 32:57.708
I know how unreliable people can be.

32:58.708 --> 33:00.166
[breathes deeply]

33:00.167 --> 33:03.208
I've learned that loyalty and courage,

33:04.208 --> 33:05.541
two qualities that are...

33:05.542 --> 33:06.625
well...

33:08.208 --> 33:09.791
not easily replicated.

33:09.792 --> 33:11.832
Sir, I don't deserve to...

33:11.833 --> 33:13.499
Um, Daniel, just shut up.

33:13.500 --> 33:15.875
Are you trying to argue yourself
out of a job?

33:18.208 --> 33:19.208
No.

33:20.375 --> 33:21.375
I'm not.

33:22.375 --> 33:23.417
I'm sorry, sir.

33:27.250 --> 33:29.458
[♪ menacing music playing]

33:30.458 --> 33:32.958
In the fullness of time,
you'll make a better man.

33:34.208 --> 33:38.417
That said, if you ever do
anything like that again,

33:39.000 --> 33:41.667
it will be the last thing
that you ever do.

33:42.708 --> 33:44.208
Do you understand?

33:47.083 --> 33:48.083
Yes, sir.

33:49.167 --> 33:50.167
Loud and clear.

33:51.875 --> 33:54.250
It'll never happen again.

33:59.042 --> 34:01.250
[indistinct chatter]

34:02.708 --> 34:03.999
[woman] Take two.

34:04.000 --> 34:05.374
[woman] Mayor Fisk, you never see him.

34:05.375 --> 34:07.832
Every week it seems like
he's involved in a new scandal.

34:07.833 --> 34:09.582
I mean,
look what just happened with the garbage.

34:09.583 --> 34:12.166
And look at all the garbage
on the street, you know.

34:12.167 --> 34:15.582
How can we trust a guy like that
who makes all of these promises

34:15.583 --> 34:17.000
to actually have our back?

34:17.833 --> 34:19.875
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

34:22.583 --> 34:23.875
[cane clacking]

34:28.375 --> 34:30.874
- [Matt] Projectile?
- [coroner] Not recovered.

34:30.875 --> 34:33.041
[Matt] 9 millimeter to the temple.
Execution style.

34:33.042 --> 34:34.542
[gun fires]

34:35.833 --> 34:38.957
Single kill shot at extreme close range
and no one found the casing?

34:38.958 --> 34:40.417
[steam hissing]

34:43.458 --> 34:45.375
[metal clanking]

34:48.500 --> 34:50.000
[cap continues clanking]

34:54.333 --> 34:55.499
[glass rattling]

34:55.500 --> 34:56.791
[car honking distantly]

34:56.792 --> 34:58.875
[glass continues rattling]

35:04.500 --> 35:05.916
[glass shatters]

35:05.917 --> 35:08.000
[♪ mysterious music playing]

35:16.500 --> 35:17.749
[glass clinking]

35:17.750 --> 35:19.833
[♪ mysterious music continues]

35:33.167 --> 35:34.167
[sniffs]

35:36.292 --> 35:38.292
[♪ ominous music playing]

35:46.167 --> 35:48.167
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

35:53.292 --> 35:55.208
[cane clacking]

36:09.167 --> 36:11.167
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

36:12.542 --> 36:14.417
[elevator whirring]

36:16.250 --> 36:18.041
[elevator thuds]

36:18.042 --> 36:19.833
- [elevator dings]
- [door rattles]

36:25.125 --> 36:26.125
[cane clacks]

36:30.792 --> 36:32.333
[electricity crackling]

36:38.833 --> 36:40.792
[water trickling]

36:47.500 --> 36:48.875
[door creaks]

36:51.708 --> 36:52.832
Hello? [echoes]

36:52.833 --> 36:54.542
[electricity crackling faintly]

37:04.583 --> 37:05.583
Christ.

37:07.833 --> 37:08.999
- I know you are in--
- [man yelling]

37:09.000 --> 37:10.582
It's me! It's me! [grunts]

37:10.583 --> 37:12.332
Frank! Frank! Frank!

37:12.333 --> 37:14.457
- It's me. It's Matthew.
- [both panting]

37:14.458 --> 37:16.458
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

37:18.708 --> 37:19.708
Goddamn it!

37:21.333 --> 37:23.374
- What're you doing here?
- How you been? Good?

37:23.375 --> 37:25.417
[Matt panting]

37:26.542 --> 37:27.583
Peachy.

37:30.083 --> 37:31.625
[Frank breathes heavily]

37:33.625 --> 37:35.083
[pills rattling]

37:36.417 --> 37:38.582
- What do you want?
- [Matt] A client of mine was shot, Frank.

37:38.583 --> 37:42.499
Guess whose logo I found
on the bullet casing?

37:42.500 --> 37:44.582
[♪ foreboding music playing]

37:44.583 --> 37:46.207
Oh, for Christ's sake.

37:46.208 --> 37:48.499
Bunch of bullshit fanboys, huh?

37:48.500 --> 37:51.375
- [sighs]
- [Matt] Yeah, and a lot of them are cops.

37:52.167 --> 37:54.166
- What does that got to do with me?
- Yeah.

37:54.167 --> 37:57.167
Nothing to do with you, right. Silly me.

37:59.458 --> 38:01.750
- Nice place you got here.
- Hmm. Appreciate that.

38:03.667 --> 38:04.792
[whistles]

38:06.333 --> 38:09.042
[Matt] Although, here's a thought.
You know you could use

38:09.875 --> 38:13.042
all this to be of service.

38:13.750 --> 38:18.083
[snorts, laughs]
Yeah. Be of service, huh?

38:19.125 --> 38:22.333
Are you... are you of service, Red?

38:22.875 --> 38:23.958
Did you serve?

38:24.958 --> 38:27.166
You prance around the city
in a Halloween costume

38:27.167 --> 38:28.666
beating the snot out of bad guys.

38:28.667 --> 38:30.666
- Hey, thank you for your service!
- [water sloshing]

38:30.667 --> 38:32.499
I mean you could help people,
you could save lives.

38:32.500 --> 38:33.792
I... I did that.

38:34.458 --> 38:36.125
I was down range, Red.

38:37.458 --> 38:38.624
Look at what it got me.

38:38.625 --> 38:41.042
Oh, I apologize. I didn't realize
you were a victim in all this.

38:42.167 --> 38:44.082
- [glass shatters]
- [objects clattering]

38:44.083 --> 38:46.374
I didn't use that pussy-ass word
my entire life,

38:46.375 --> 38:48.166
you don't put it in my mouth,
you understand that?

38:48.167 --> 38:49.832
All right, so you tell me
what's going on, buddy.

38:49.833 --> 38:51.541
What're you doing down here
day after day,

38:51.542 --> 38:52.999
- just hiding out?
- I ain't hiding from shit!

38:53.000 --> 38:54.832
- You walked in, I'm right here.
- Plotting your next kill?

38:54.833 --> 38:56.874
- You're goddamn right.
- Great. How is that working out?

38:56.875 --> 38:59.542
You wanna go out there on the street,
have at it!

39:00.042 --> 39:03.958
But I do not have time
for your candy-ass hero shit.

39:04.583 --> 39:06.541
- Is that clear?
- Yeah. Loud and clear.

39:06.542 --> 39:09.042
- [Frank] Yeah?
- Sorry to waste your time.

39:11.583 --> 39:12.583
Yeah.

39:13.792 --> 39:16.124
- I'll tell you what I think, Red.
- Tell me. Tell me what you think.

39:16.125 --> 39:18.000
I don't think you came here for my help.

39:19.917 --> 39:21.042
[Matt sighs]

39:22.750 --> 39:24.416
See. I think you want my permission.

39:24.417 --> 39:25.542
[chuckles]

39:26.875 --> 39:30.250
You wanna get your hands on somebody, huh?
Wanna hurt 'em.

39:31.083 --> 39:34.958
Maybe you're a little bit scared.
A little scared about what that means.

39:37.042 --> 39:39.416
[chuckles] That's an interesting take.
I like it.

39:39.417 --> 39:41.832
But, uh, yeah, no. Sorry, buddy.
Way off on that one.

39:41.833 --> 39:44.999
Yeah, you're so full of shit, Counselor.
So full of shit.

39:45.000 --> 39:46.457
- You're guilty.
- Excuse me?

39:46.458 --> 39:49.250
Yeah, that guilt, that shame,
that's my home, Red.

39:50.042 --> 39:52.833
And I can see it on you,
I can smell it on you. It's all over you.

39:53.708 --> 39:55.124
I'm gonna come back another day, Frank,

39:55.125 --> 39:56.333
maybe catch you at a better time.

39:57.792 --> 40:00.457
You come at me with that horseshit
about saving lives.

40:00.458 --> 40:02.582
How 'bout that friend of yours?
You save his life?

40:02.583 --> 40:04.666
[♪ somber music playing]

40:04.667 --> 40:06.375
You lost him, didn't you, Red?

40:09.750 --> 40:11.874
- It's not about him.
- Then say his name.

40:11.875 --> 40:14.333
It's not about him. It's not about him.

40:15.458 --> 40:17.666
Ah, for Christ's sake, say his name!

40:17.667 --> 40:20.708
- [breath trembling]
- Say his name, you coward, say his name!

40:21.167 --> 40:22.458
It's not about him?

40:22.958 --> 40:24.707
You hate yourself. It's eating you up

40:24.708 --> 40:27.249
because you ain't done
a goddamn thing about it, so--

40:27.250 --> 40:29.082
- [grunting]
- Oh, oh.

40:29.083 --> 40:30.832
Goddamn it. Goddamn you. [breathes deeply]

40:30.833 --> 40:32.583
- [grunts]
- [Matt breathes rapidly]

40:34.458 --> 40:37.124
[exhales] Sorry, I apologize.

40:37.125 --> 40:38.542
What are you sorry for?

40:40.708 --> 40:42.542
First honest thing you did, Red.

40:44.125 --> 40:45.458
- It's not about him.
- No.

40:46.000 --> 40:48.208
Okay? [breathing heavily]

40:49.667 --> 40:50.833
It's all about him.

40:53.500 --> 40:54.875
He talks to you, dudn't he?

40:57.042 --> 40:58.167
You hear his voice.

40:58.958 --> 41:00.083
You do, don't you?

41:01.125 --> 41:03.833
[softly] Every time I stop moving,
I still hear my little boy.

41:05.750 --> 41:06.750
I see him.

41:09.292 --> 41:10.750
And I hear his voice.

41:12.917 --> 41:14.292
He says, "Get 'em, Daddy.

41:15.583 --> 41:17.500
"Every last single one of 'em, get 'em."

41:18.167 --> 41:19.917
That's why I do what I do.

41:21.167 --> 41:23.749
And that's why I see it in you.
That's why I see it in you

41:23.750 --> 41:25.749
because you know
you didn't do a goddamn thing

41:25.750 --> 41:27.082
and it's gonna keep eating at you.

41:27.083 --> 41:29.291
It's gonna keep eating, and eating,
and eating.

41:29.292 --> 41:31.457
There's no getting away with it,
you understand?

41:31.458 --> 41:33.125
[♪ melancholy music playing]

41:33.250 --> 41:34.500
[breathing shakily]

41:37.167 --> 41:38.166
I ran him down.

41:38.167 --> 41:39.499
Oh, for Christ's sake!

41:39.500 --> 41:41.124
I did what I had to do.

41:41.125 --> 41:42.874
And I let the system
take care of the rest--

41:42.875 --> 41:45.207
- Oh! You and your Goddamn sy--
- [muttering indistinctly]

41:45.208 --> 41:47.125
You and your Goddamn system!

41:47.708 --> 41:48.707
Christ!

41:48.708 --> 41:52.124
So what now? Every day
Bullseye goes to the chow hole,

41:52.125 --> 41:56.124
eats his slop, you know he gets
to breathe the same air that you breathe.

41:56.125 --> 41:58.708
- You feel good about that?
- He got life!

41:59.917 --> 42:01.917
[♪ melancholy music continues]

42:08.333 --> 42:11.458
How 'bout old Foggy? He get life?

42:13.833 --> 42:15.292
Foggy... [sniffles]

42:18.208 --> 42:19.208
He was the...

42:20.083 --> 42:22.042
kindest, purest soul I ever met.

42:22.958 --> 42:24.458
And guys like you and me,

42:25.208 --> 42:30.000
we can work a lifetime
and never measure up to his decency.

42:37.042 --> 42:38.125
Goodbye, Frank.

42:50.583 --> 42:52.625
[Fisk breathes deeply]

42:56.000 --> 43:00.332
[smacks lips] So,
when Dr. Glenn asked to talk--

43:00.333 --> 43:02.125
She asked if you felt safe with me.

43:05.042 --> 43:06.208
I assumed.

43:06.917 --> 43:09.667
It's what a prudent psychiatrist
would ask.

43:10.292 --> 43:11.542
I told her I did...

43:13.083 --> 43:14.208
and I wasn't lying.

43:14.917 --> 43:16.832
Well, I'm glad you feel that way.

43:16.833 --> 43:17.958
[Vanessa] I do.

43:18.875 --> 43:20.000
But, Wilson...

43:23.125 --> 43:24.167
Should I?

43:29.250 --> 43:30.750
When I was a boy,

43:31.417 --> 43:35.083
I learned by watching my father.

43:36.125 --> 43:37.792
How to shake a man's hand.

43:39.000 --> 43:42.207
How to know when someone
intends to cheat you.

43:42.208 --> 43:44.542
I learned the power of persuasion.

43:46.167 --> 43:48.833
How to move men's minds...

43:52.458 --> 43:54.250
Or break their bodies.

43:56.042 --> 43:57.332
But forgiveness...

43:57.333 --> 43:59.417
[♪ somber music playing]

44:01.417 --> 44:03.208
That wasn't a part of who he was.

44:06.167 --> 44:09.708
No. I am trying.

44:11.750 --> 44:15.374
I would like for things
to be the way they were.

44:15.375 --> 44:18.292
I understand that
that may not be possible.

44:20.042 --> 44:21.250
People change.

44:24.583 --> 44:26.917
I'm not the same woman
I was when you left.

44:28.125 --> 44:29.417
No, you aren't, are you?

44:30.958 --> 44:33.458
You're something even more extraordinary.

44:36.750 --> 44:37.792
[door closes]

44:38.458 --> 44:41.582
If I didn't know any better,
I'd think you were trying to avoid me.

44:41.583 --> 44:42.874
[sighs] I'm so sorry.

44:42.875 --> 44:44.582
I just got pulled
into another meeting.

44:44.583 --> 44:46.499
You don't have to be sorry.

44:46.500 --> 44:47.583
Really?

44:48.375 --> 44:49.374
Maybe a tiny bit.

44:49.375 --> 44:50.792
[laughs]

44:51.458 --> 44:52.832
It's funny how I...

44:52.833 --> 44:54.416
[breathes deeply]

44:54.417 --> 44:56.499
When I'm not sleeping over,
I don't worry about you.

44:56.500 --> 44:59.707
But you come home late one night
and my mind is spinning.

44:59.708 --> 45:01.832
I mean, "What if he fell
into the subway tracks?

45:01.833 --> 45:04.082
- "Maybe somebody kidnapped him."
- Kidnapped?

45:04.083 --> 45:05.374
"Maybe he needed a Heimlich...

45:05.375 --> 45:07.000
- [chuckles]
- "...and there was no one to give it."

45:09.083 --> 45:11.624
- I'm excellent at the Heimlich.
- Oh, yeah?

45:11.625 --> 45:13.582
- Mmm-hmm.
- Well, I am sorry.

45:13.583 --> 45:16.291
I mean, I'm not sorry,
I'm sorry you know, whatever. Just...

45:16.292 --> 45:17.624
[breathes deeply]

45:17.625 --> 45:19.167
One of those days, I guess.

45:20.125 --> 45:24.958
A client who was proven innocent still
ends up dead and nobody seems to care.

45:26.875 --> 45:28.374
I know, I'm sorry about that, Matt.

45:28.375 --> 45:32.249
Another client's serving time at Rikers
for stealing a bag of caramel corn.

45:32.250 --> 45:33.624
Sounds a bit excessive.

45:33.625 --> 45:34.833
[Matt snorts]

45:36.417 --> 45:38.042
You ever feel like you're, uh,

45:38.875 --> 45:41.125
pushing a rock up a hill

45:42.333 --> 45:45.583
and there's a bunch of people on
the other side pushing it back. [chuckles]

45:48.417 --> 45:49.499
How was your day?

45:49.500 --> 45:50.707
Oh, you know...

45:50.708 --> 45:52.207
[jacket thuds]

45:52.208 --> 45:56.082
A few garden variety neurotics
slash depressives

45:56.083 --> 45:59.791
plus a not so garden variety couple
in crisis?

45:59.792 --> 46:01.916
None of which you can tell me about.

46:01.917 --> 46:05.457
Well, you know, I can tell you
pretty much anything you wanna know.

46:05.458 --> 46:07.082
- Really?
- [Heather] Hmm...

46:07.083 --> 46:09.417
- I'd just have to kill you.
- [chuckles]

46:10.500 --> 46:13.750
You know, I got pretty used
to coming home to an empty apartment.

46:14.667 --> 46:15.791
And now?

46:15.792 --> 46:18.000
And now I can't imagine you
not being here.

46:20.792 --> 46:21.833
Good answer.

46:25.042 --> 46:26.416
[police siren blaring]

46:26.417 --> 46:28.083
- [car honking]
- [car passing]

46:30.333 --> 46:32.832
[train rattling]

46:32.833 --> 46:35.000
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

46:39.083 --> 46:41.292
[footsteps thudding]

46:42.625 --> 46:44.625
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

47:16.208 --> 47:17.708
[door latch clinks]

47:18.542 --> 47:19.791
[door thuds]

47:19.792 --> 47:21.875
[♪ foreboding music playing]

47:33.250 --> 47:35.250
[♪ dramatic music playing]

47:47.333 --> 47:49.500
[cane whooshing]

47:53.125 --> 47:56.416
[man, weakly]
Please... Mr. Fisk...

47:56.417 --> 47:58.457
[chains rattling]

47:58.458 --> 47:59.583
Mayor Fisk.

48:01.792 --> 48:03.041
[chain rattling]

48:03.042 --> 48:07.917
I was told forgiveness
is the highest form of love.

48:09.667 --> 48:10.750
I wonder...

48:12.250 --> 48:15.124
would you agree with that, Adam?

48:15.125 --> 48:16.333
[Adam breathing shakily]

48:19.250 --> 48:20.791
[chain whooshing]

48:20.792 --> 48:22.042
[grunts]

48:22.542 --> 48:24.833
[Adam] Please... Fisk!

48:25.667 --> 48:26.917
[grunts softly]

48:28.917 --> 48:30.000
[Adam, weakly] Please.

48:30.833 --> 48:33.124
- Please!
- [chains rattling]

48:33.125 --> 48:34.583
Let me out!

48:42.583 --> 48:44.708
[train rattling]

48:47.542 --> 48:49.542
[♪ mysterious music playing]

48:53.333 --> 48:55.250
[♪ eerie music playing]

49:04.542 --> 49:05.957
[metal clangs]

49:05.958 --> 49:08.417
- [mechanical whirring]
- [man groans]

49:09.667 --> 49:11.167
[screaming]

49:17.417 --> 49:19.458
[♪ dramatic music playing]

50:00.083 --> 50:01.582
[♪ dramatic music fades]

50:01.583 --> 50:03.667
[♪ foreboding music playing]

50:26.708 --> 50:28.708
[♪ foreboding music continues]

51:45.542 --> 51:47.333
[♪ music ends]
